From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:27:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 292/342] realtekwifi: USB Tx aggregation and a longer send
 queue on the RTL8822B

Up to 8 data frames now share a bulk OUT transfer, after rtw88's
rtw_usb_tx_agg_skb(), and the send queue holds 256 frames instead of 50. Each was
a limit: USB was busy all the time at one frame or three per transfer, and the
queue's overflow cost TCP its speed. A drop per 2,000 frames holds a connection at
about 22 MB/s with this round trip, and that's where it sat with room in the chip
and CPU to spare.

Upload 12.8 to 26.4 MB/s on channel 64, and 17.3 to 31.7 on channel 136, against a
laptop, with a 1 MB socket buffer; download the same. No restart in 37.6 GB. At 8
frames USB is about 94% busy, so it's near its limit of 36 MB/s; 12 frames gave
no more.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
